<BaseLayout title="Sponsor GitRacer" description="Put your developer product beside shareable GitHub contribution races with a clean, fixed sponsor placement.">
  <article class="content-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">sponsor slots · opening soon</span>
    <h1>Be beside the race, not in the way.</h1>
    <p class="lede">GitRacer’s desktop sponsor rails are prominent, fixed, and deliberately calm. The audience is developers comparing real public GitHub activity—without an ad network following them around afterward.</p>
    <div class="callout">Launch inventory: six desktop rail cards and one responsive mobile placement. Direct placements only.</div>
    <h2>What sponsors will receive</h2>
    <ul><li>A name, logo, short line, and destination URL.</li><li>Aggregate cookieless impressions and clicks by placement.</li><li>Visible labeling and no dark patterns.</li><li>Monthly reporting from PostHog web analytics.</li></ul>
    <h2>What we will not sell</h2>
    <p>No visitor identities, email lists, session recordings, cross-site profiles, or pixel access. Sponsor reporting is aggregate.</p>
    <h2>Reserve a launch slot</h2>
    <p>Email <a href="mailto:hello@gitracer.io">hello@gitracer.io</a> with your product, target URL, and preferred launch month. Pricing will be published once the site has enough traffic to make the numbers meaningful.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
